we have some breaking news this morning  because the second round of rescue  operations in Thailand is working to  save more members of a youth soccer team  and their coach they've been trapped in  a cave since June 23rd now one boy was  taken from the cave this morning and he  is at the hospital a 6th and 7th person  were just taken out on stretchers and  are about to be transported to the  hospital the first four boys were  rescued yesterday the local governor  says there are concerns about more rain  and flooding Ben Tracy is in chiang rai  thailand with the urgent push to rescue  the boys the clock is ticking Ben good  morning good morning it sure is and you  know it's been surprisingly dry here  today there's so they're certainly  trying to seize the moment get as many  of these boys out of this cave as  possible before it potentially floods  again so the second phase of this rescue  operation appears to be going very well  it appears also to be going very quickly  now while the divers are inside the cave  guiding these Boyd's boys to safety they  are still pumping water out to make sure  that that journey is as safe as possible  despite some heavy rain last night  officials say water levels inside the  cave did not rise much particularly  helping this effort it's speeding it up  now if the cave were to flood the  remaining boys could be stuck on a piece  of land that is only about 100 square  feet that concern is part of what  prompted the risky rescue operation to  begin now to get out of the cave each  boy is tethered to a diver who is  following a rope with another diver  trailing behind the two and a half mile  journey takes about takes several hours  as many as eight hours one of the most  difficult areas is a pinch point that is  just 15 inches across where the boys  have to separate from their diver to fit  through now officials here are telling  us that the entire rescue operation to  get everybody out of that cave could  take another 24 to 48 hours but they are  clearly ahead of schedule and it is very  good news here today to see so many of  these boys coming out of this cave gale  it is Ben Tracy it's great great great  news and we are all waiting and hoping  and praying it continues thanks a lot
 

